# grand-rounds federation — local gated-data guard.
#
# The unrecoverable failure mode for this federation is committing gated
# clinical data (or anything derived from it). Gated inputs and all
# intermediate/output artifacts live OUTSIDE the checkout, reached only via
# $MVA_DATA_DIR / $MVA_WORK_DIR / $MVA_OUT_DIR. This file is a local
# belt-and-braces guard; tools/check-no-gated-data.sh is the enforced gate
# (it runs on CI, where the agentis runtime is absent by design).
#
# The synthetic, gated-data-free fixtures under baseline/fixtures/ are the one
# exception — they carry synthetic sample names and no HPO literals, and their
# purity is asserted by baseline/demo-baseline.sh.

*.vcf
*.vcf.*
*.bcf
*.bcf.*
*.fastq
*.fastq.*
*.fq
*.fq.*
*.bam
*.bam.*
*.cram
*.cram.*
*.docx
*.gtf
*.gtf.*
*.fa
*.fa.gz
*.fna
*.fna.gz
*.fai
*.obo
data/
work/
refdata/
out/
# Submission CSVs, under any name. The runbook encourages renaming to take-N,
# so pinning the shipped prefix alone left every rename stageable.
agentis-federation_*.csv
take-*.csv
*submission*.csv

# Derived analysis artifacts the pipeline writes. These carry coordinates but
# no forbidden extension, so nothing stopped them being staged; the leak guard
# now has a coordinate needle as well, and this is the belt to its braces.
refuted.tsv
panel-review.tsv
lens-*.tsv

# Agentis runtime state. `agentis init` creates baseline/.agentis (holding an
# Ed25519 keypair) and baseline/examples/; install.sh may park a broken stub as
# .agentis.broken-<timestamp>. None of it belongs in the bundle, and a private
# key must never become stageable.
.agentis/
.agentis.broken-*/
baseline/examples/
*.key

# Named, like the guard's allowlist: a NEW file under fixtures/ is not
# automatically un-ignored just because it sits in that directory.
!baseline/fixtures/README.md
!baseline/fixtures/mini.fa
!baseline/fixtures/panel.gtf
!baseline/fixtures/phenotype-source.txt
!baseline/fixtures/proband.vcf
